199: Frontend modules define their entry point in `src/index.ts`.
200: 
201: ```ts
202: import { defineConfigSchema, getAsyncLifecycle, getSyncLifecycle } from "@openmrs/esm-framework";
203: import { configSchema } from "./config-schema";
204: import ActivePrescriptionsSummary from "./active-prescriptions-summary.component";
205: import { moduleName } from "./constants";
206: 
207: export const importTranslation = require.context("../translations", false, /.json$/, "lazy");
208: 
209: const options = {
210:   featureName: "active-prescriptions",
211:   moduleName,
212: };
213: 
214: export function startupApp() {
215:   defineConfigSchema(moduleName, configSchema);
216: }
217: 
218: export const root = getAsyncLifecycle(() => import("./root.component"), options);
219: 
220: export const activePrescriptionsSummary = getSyncLifecycle(ActivePrescriptionsSummary, options);
221: ```
222: 
223: This file is the entry point of the frontend module. It is the first file that gets executed when the frontend module gets loaded. It is responsible for setting up the frontend module and exporting the module’s configuration. Specifically, in this example:
224: 
225: - It exports an `importTranslation` function which is used to load the module’s translations.

